"""Editorial questions for collectibles, antiques, and making."""

from review_angle_plans import audit, revise_domain


ANTIQUES = """history_origins|How a Collecting Category Formed|Who began valuing one class of objects and under what criteria?|Compare dated catalogs, collections, trade records, and source-community views.
famous_examples|A Famous Antique Reexamined|What do an identified object's material and ownership records establish?|Study catalog, condition, provenance, and disputed claims.
hidden_stories|People Behind the Object|Whose maker, user, dealer, conservator, or source-community role is omitted?|Use object records and attributed accounts with custody context.
beginner_explainers|Reading an Antique Listing|Which claims about date, maker, condition, and provenance can be checked?|Use a real listing and comparable object records without purchase advice.
advanced_concepts|Authenticity Beyond a Signature|How do material, technique, documentation, and comparison support attribution?|Compare independent analyses and uncertainty for one item.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|An Object With a Gap in Custody|Which records might resolve one disputed ownership interval?|Trace auction, inventory, export, family, and museum documentation.
technology_innovation|A Conservation Test|What could one imaging or material test reveal without damaging an object?|Compare method validation, limits, and documented interpretation.
people_personalities|A Collector's Decision|How did one named collector shape what survived and what was excluded?|Use inventories, correspondence, acquisitions, and affected communities.
major_events|A Collection Changes Hands|What happened when one group of objects was sold, seized, donated, or returned?|Build a dated ownership and legal timeline, acknowledging contested claims.
how_it_works|From Find to Catalog|How is one antique identified, documented, conserved, and displayed?|Follow actual institutional records and distinguish catalog opinion from proof.
rise_fall|A Collectible's Market Fashion|Why did interest in one object class rise or fall?|Compare production, scarcity, collecting institutions, and dated sales with bias.
then_vs_now|One Object, Two Interpretations|How did cataloging or community meaning change over time?|Compare old and new records, evidence, and stakeholder voices.
future_developments|A Proposed Reattribution or Return|What evidence and consultation would a new decision require?|Specify custody, material analysis, legal context, community interests, and uncertainty.
myths_vs_facts|An Antique Legend Checked|Does a claimed maker, owner, or age match the record?|Trace earliest claim, physical evidence, and independent documentation.
documentary_stories|An Object's Provenance Trail|How did one collectible move from use to present custody?|Create a dated record of owners, transactions, treatments, and gaps.
source_trail|The Citation Behind a Catalog Entry|Which original document supports a repeated object claim?|Trace inventory numbers, photographs, dates, and source reliability.
material_evidence|An Object's Fabric as Record|What do materials and wear reveal about making or later alteration?|Compare conservation study with provenance and use context.
chronology_dispute|Dating a Collectible|Why do experts assign different dates to one object?|Compare maker marks, materials, style, documented ownership, and uncertainty.
ordinary_lives|An Antique's Original Use|How did ordinary people use one object before it became collectible?|Use period documents and source-community accounts, not collector value alone.
power_and_institutions|Who Defines an Object's Status?|Which museum, market, state, or community has authority over one item's display?|Compare legal rights, institutional policy, and ethical claims.
trade_and_exchange|An Object's Route to Market|What can transaction and transport records show about one antique?|Trace known legs and avoid filling gaps with assumptions.
language_and_labels|What Does the Label Hide?|How do names like tribal, primitive, or rare distort an object's context?|Compare original terms, catalog history, and preferred community language.
maps_and_borders|Origin and Border Claims|How did changing borders or export rules affect one item's custody?|Date each jurisdiction and document rather than applying present borders backward.
conflicting_accounts|Two Provenance Narratives|Where do seller, collector, and source-community accounts differ?|Compare records, incentives, dates, and missing testimony.
preservation_bias|What Was Collected?|Which everyday objects were ignored while prestigious ones survived?|Examine collection policy, market demand, and community loss.
turning_point_test|Did a Discovery Change Attribution?|What new evidence actually changed expert opinion?|Compare catalog before and after, technical result, and competing readings.
legacy_and_memory|An Antique in Public Memory|How do display and collecting affect community memory?|Use visitor and source-community voices with museum records.
field_community_ownership|A Community's Claim|What evidence and values underlie one claim to control or access?|Read custody and consultation records and attribute contested positions.
field_object_provenance|Documenting Each Custody Link|Which transfers in an object's history are verifiable?|List dates, people, documents, and unresolved intervals.
field_living_practice|An Object Still in Use|How does current practice change the meaning of a collected item?|Ask practitioners with permission; avoid treating it only as an artifact.
field_conservation_choice|Repair or Preserve Evidence?|Which treatment best balances stability and historical information?|Compare condition, options, reversibility, and stakeholder wishes.
field_cultural_translation|An Object Between Contexts|What meaning changed when an item entered a different collection or market?|Compare original use, label, display, and source-community interpretation."""


DIY = """history_origins|A Making Practice's Lineage|Which materials, tools, and communities shaped one craft?|Compare dated objects, manuals, maker testimony, and transmission.
famous_examples|A Maker Project Reexamined|What did one widely shared build actually require and deliver?|Compare bill of materials, time, skills, tests, and later repairs.
hidden_stories|People Behind a DIY Design|Whose pattern, repair, or community knowledge was left uncredited?|Trace source design, collaborators, licenses, and attributed accounts.
beginner_explainers|Planning a Small Making Project|Which purpose, dimensions, materials, tools, and checks must be defined?|Use a low-risk example and identify when qualified supervision is needed.
advanced_concepts|Strength, Tolerance, and Fit|How do measurement error and material variation affect one safe project?|Compare plans, prototypes, tests, and failure limits without structural advice.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|Why a Build Failed|Which documented causes explain one project's unexpected result?|Compare materials, dimensions, process records, and testing conditions.
technology_innovation|A New Making Tool|Did one digital or manual tool improve quality, access, or waste?|Use matched prototypes and account for learning, cost, and safety.
people_personalities|A Maker's Design Choice|Why did one craftsperson choose a particular material or process?|Use sketches, interviews, prototypes, and local tradition.
major_events|A Repair Movement or Policy|How did one dated event change access to tools, parts, or knowledge?|Compare participation, costs, laws, and maker experience.
how_it_works|From Brief to Tested Object|How does a safe project move through design, prototype, verification, and revision?|Trace one low-risk example at conceptual level, not hazardous procedures.
rise_fall|A DIY Trend's Lifecycle|Why did one project type spread and then change?|Compare tool access, price, online communities, safety, and durability.
then_vs_now|Making the Same Object Across Eras|How did materials, time, tools, and repairability change?|Compare equivalent objects and measured performance.
future_developments|A Proposed Community Workshop|What evidence would show whether a new making program serves its users?|Define access, training, costs, safety, output, and long-term support.
myths_vs_facts|A DIY Hack Checked|Does a viral shortcut meet the claimed cost, durability, or safety outcome?|Compare independent testing and official guidance; avoid repeating risky steps.
documentary_stories|One Project Through Revisions|How did a maker move from need to final object?|Build a dated account of prototypes, tests, failures, and user feedback.
creative_brief|Who Needs the Object?|Which user, budget, space, and aesthetic requirements shaped one build?|Compare brief, alternatives, prototype, and user evaluation.
materials_and_tools|Choosing a Material|How do strength, availability, cost, toxicity, and repair affect one choice?|Use product data and safe independent tests for a defined object.
process_breakdown|The Parts of a Build|Which stages created most effort or error in one documented project?|Use time logs, material records, and quality checks without unsafe instructions.
composition_choice|Pattern and Form|How did layout, joinery, or pattern choice affect function and appearance?|Compare prototypes and observed use, keeping structural claims qualified.
collaborative_authorship|Who Contributed to the Pattern?|Which designers, testers, and community makers improved one design?|Trace versions, credits, license, and feedback.
adaptation_across_media|A Pattern Becomes a Tutorial|What changes when a workshop design is taught by video or print?|Compare missing context, tool assumptions, accessibility, and safety notes.
audience_reception|How Makers Used the Plan|Which adaptations and problems appeared in documented attempts?|Sample varied users and avoid treating comments as a performance test.
cultural_context|A Craft in Its Community|What meanings and rules shape one making tradition?|Use attributed practitioners and respect restricted knowledge.
preservation_restoration|Repairing a Handmade Object|Which intervention preserves function and maker evidence?|Compare condition, materials, options, and reversibility.
rights_and_attribution|Sharing a Design|Which licenses, patents, and cultural protocols govern one pattern?|Check jurisdiction and original creator before reuse.
style_comparison|Two Makers, One Object|How did two approaches solve a similar function?|Match materials, tools, skill, cost, and durability.
creative_failure|A Prototype That Did Not Work|What did one failed attempt reveal about the original assumptions?|Use measurements, user feedback, and documented revision.
field_material_selection|A Material for the Job|Which properties matter for one object's intended use?|Compare manufacturer data, tests, availability, and end-of-life.
field_tool_control|Tool Choice and Risk|Which tool capabilities and safeguards affected one project?|Use manufacturer and safety guidance at overview level, without risky procedures.
field_pattern_design|A Pattern's Fit Across Users|How did one pattern account for size and user variation?|Compare dimensions, prototypes, and accessibility feedback.
field_repairability|Designed to Be Fixed|How easily can parts be accessed, replaced, or reused?|Compare actual repairs, part availability, fasteners, and costs.
field_craft_lineage|Learning From Earlier Makers|Which documented techniques and communities shaped one design?|Trace source patterns, teachers, adaptations, and credit."""


if __name__ == "__main__":
    revise_domain("084", "084_collectibles_antiques", ANTIQUES,
                  "Collectibles and antiques through object identification, provenance, original use, market claims, conservation, and community or ownership disputes.",
                  "identified object catalogs, inventories and sale records, technical and condition reports, custody and export documents, maker records, and attributed source-community accounts",
                  "Name object, date, material, jurisdiction, and custody. Separate market value from historical significance, attribute contested ownership, and verify current trade and export rules before production.")
    revise_domain("085", "085_diy_making", DIY,
                  "DIY and making through documented design briefs, material and tool choices, prototypes, tests, maker credit, safe access, repair, and craft lineage.",
                  "dated maker plans and versions, manufacturer material data, prototype and independent test records, product safety guidance, licenses, and attributed craft-practitioner accounts",
                  "Bound projects to low-risk examples. Avoid hazardous tool, electrical, chemical, or structural instructions; check current manufacturer and local safety rules, and state when qualified work is required.")
    rows = audit()
    print(f"Plans: {len(rows)}; reviewed question designs: {sum(r['status'] == 'editorial_question_reviewed' for r in rows)}")
